 "structural_change": "S81-TILES2 10-17: four-tile re-split of the KP4 decoder cluster ot_s81_kp4_dec (replaces s81lk_kp4_deca / decb, REJECTED at their CTS gates: 259.2 um tiles, SRAM in the middle, clock on the S face; TT insertion 307-455 / 295-417 ps, spread 148 / 122 ps).  Cluster 2 x 2: dsyn SW (PMA in W), ddly NW, dchn SE, dout NE (beats out E); every seam registered at both pins.  Bit-exact vs the 33a35eb7d two-tile decoder on every output and cycle (tb_s81_kp4_eq: RTL same cycle, hardware view with all tile pin registers = reference + 2 cycles; mutants DMUT 2 / 3 and a one-short word seam FAIL).  dout: the 32 x 546 correction-mask SRAM delay (DC = 9), corrected words straight from the two read ports, fixed-offset beat select; macro at (43.2, 43.2) R0 on the 43.2 lattice against the N face (20.5 um channel), one std-cell band S (41 um) holding the cw pin registers and the beat logic; R0 puts the macro read port on its W edge beside d_q.  d_q full W face (from ddly, 3.9/um), cw + decision full S face (from dchn, 2.3/um), q_* E face (4.5/um), clk E face beside the S band.  ~3.4k sinks.  Aspect 1.69: a single-macro tile.",
